# IAI

This repo root is the Max-Vitter working folder (`work/2026/max-vitter`). Every request about a client site goes through IAI before design or code.

Do not jump from a raw brief to pages, Webflow, WordPress, or a visual mock. Do not invent brand, audience, or features the client did not give.

## Pass 1 — brain

Write or update `specs/01-brain.md`.

- Facts the client actually said
- Constraints (budget, CMS, languages, deadline, hosting, brand assets)
- Unknowns and contradictions
- What the site must do on the first visit (one sentence)
- What we will not decide until the brief is complete

If the brief is empty, stop after Pass 1 and wait. Do not fill gaps with generic agency copy.

## Pass 2 — specs

Fill the files in `specs/` in this order:

1. Concept
2. Structure (pages, modules, CMS)
3. Visual
4. Motion (scroll, windows, transitions)
5. Platform (only after motion and CMS needs are clear)

Specs are the source of truth. Implementation follows them. If a later request conflicts with a spec, update the spec first, then the work.

## Pass 3 — voice

Before anything leaves the repo (copy, README, spec prose, UI strings):

- Cut filler, slogans, and “AI English/Ukrainian”
- Ban: інноваційний, безшовний, занурення, наступний рівень, у сучасному світі, унікальний досвід, tailor-made, cutting-edge, seamless, elevate, unlock, dive in
- Prefer short sentences, concrete nouns, present tense
- Keep the studio register: direct, dry, Ukrainian unless the client writes in another language
- Do not leave process notes, model names, or “as an AI” in client files

## Build

After specs exist: implement only what the spec names. Do not add sections “for completeness.”
